{
  "_comment": [
    "Shared golden cases for the grievance case workflow (GrievanceCaseWorkflow.cs). The API runs every case against the domain (Apex.Hrms.Domain.Tests, GrievanceTransitionCasesTests); the Angular demo mock is meant to run the same file. Fictional data only.",
    "Shape: { _comment, cases: Case[] }. Every case has a unique 'name', a starting 'case', an 'action', an 'actor', an optional 'input', and either 'expected' or 'expectedError'.",
    "Clock: today is 2026-11-18 and every step happens at 2026-11-18T08:00:00Z.",
    "Actors: submitter = { userId 10, employeeId 100, name 'TST Submitter', role Submitter }, management = { 20, 200, 'TST HR Manager', Management }, investigator = { 30, 300, 'TST Investigator', Investigator }, reviewer = { 40, 400, 'TST Reviewer', Reviewer }. The submitter is never identified in what a case records: on a named case as { userId null, employeeId null, name 'Submitter', role Submitter } (screens show the name from the case's submitter record), on an anonymous case as { userId null, employeeId null, name 'Anonymous submitter', role Submitter }.",
    "case: { status, isAnonymous (false), returnStatus (only for AwaitingEmployeeResponse: UnderReview, Assigned or UnderInvestigation), hasLead (whether the case has an active lead; the lead is employee 300; reached through Assigned; on a Reopened case: the lead it had before the reopening, which the reopening ended, so it has no active lead), members (employee ids of active Member assignments), proposedBy (who made the pending proposal of a ResolutionProposed case: investigator when there is a lead, management otherwise), reopenedFrom (Closed or Rejected), isEscalated, legalHold, archived, subjectEmployeeId, reassignedAfterReopen (Assigned reached by closing a case with its lead, reopening it, which ends every assignment, and assigning the same lead again) }. Missing fields take the defaults in brackets, null or false. A runner may build the state directly; the API test reaches it through the real transitions.",
    "The draft of every case: category id 0 (active, allows anonymous, 14 default target days), subject 'Repeated unfair shift assignments', description 'My shifts are changed without notice every week.', no incident date. On the way to the starting status: acknowledge with priority Medium, reject with reason 'TST rejected on the way.', reopen with 'TST reopened on the way.', request info with 'TST question on the way?', propose 'TST resolution on the way.' and approve by the reviewer; escalation (isEscalated) and the subject (subjectEmployeeId) are set right after submission. A named submitter's placement { company 1, branch 2, department 3, position 4 } is offered at submission.",
    "action and input: submit { declarationAccepted (true), categoryActive (true), categoryAllowsAnonymous (true) }; acknowledge { priority, targetResolutionDate (null = default), defaultTargetDays }; reject { reason }; startReview; assign { investigatorEmployeeId, role, reason }; unassign { investigatorEmployeeId }; startInvestigation; requestInfo { message }; respond { message }; postSubmitterMessage { message }; postTeamMessage { message }; proposeResolution { summary }; approveResolution { visibleToSubmitter, comment }; rejectResolution { reason }; close; reopen { reason }; escalate { reason }; archive. A text input '<field>Length': n stands for a text of n letters 'x'. The named submitter (employee 100) is passed as the submitter an investigator must not be; an anonymous case passes none.",
    "expected (only the fields present are compared): status, returnStatus, isEscalated, archived, hasPlacement, priority, targetResolutionDate, rejectionReason, resolutionVisibleToSubmitter, proposalDecision, assignment { investigatorEmployeeId, role }, endedAssignment (employee id), endedAssignments (the employee ids a reopening unassigned, in order), message { direction, kind } or null (no message), history: the new history entries in order, each { action, fromStatus, toStatus, actorRole, visibleToSubmitter, reason } plus actorName, actorUserId and actorEmployeeId where given. An empty history means the step wrote none.",
    "expectedError: { type (Validation, Conflict or Forbidden, as AppError), fields (the fieldErrors keys of a Validation failure) }. Messages are the API's and are not compared. A failed step changes nothing."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
